IMPORT prelude

-- Corporate Service Providers Act 2024 (Singapore) -- what a corporate service is (s 2), the ban on carrying on that business
-- unregistered and the deemed registration of accounting entities (s 7), the renewal window and the grounds on which the
-- Registrar must refuse registration (ss 8 to 11), the 14-day notice duty (s 12), who must provide the service (s 14), nominee
-- directors (s 16), customer due diligence (s 17), regulatory action (ss 19, 21), appeals (s 23), the offence penalties (ss 7, 12,
-- 16, 17, 25), composition (s 27) and the transitional grace for existing businesses (s 42).
--
-- Edition: the Act as enacted (No. 22 of 2024), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CSPA2024.txt. The deposit is NOT
-- a 2020 Revised Edition consolidation; its retrieval record calls it the SSO "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026", and no
-- amendment annotations appear in the text. The commencement date (s 1: by Gazette notification) is not in the deposit.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 5 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a corporate service
-- provider, a qualified individual or their client actually meets. Not encoded: the meaning of "accounting service" (s 3) beyond
-- its use in one service type, administration and registers (ss 5, 6), modification of conditions (s 13), deemed qualified
-- individuals (s 15), cancellation on the s 18 and s 20 grounds, the s 22 procedure, interest and recovery (s 28), the liability of
-- officers and partners (ss 29, 30), jurisdiction, publication, service and exemptions (ss 31 to 34), the consequential amendments
-- (Part 8) and the filing-agent transitional rules (ss 43 to 45). Everything left to regulations (the "qualified individual"
-- criteria, the prescribed course, the fit-and-proper factors, the customer due diligence measures, fees) is a bare input.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Corporate Service Providers Act 2024 -- registration`

§§ `2 -- corporate service`

-- s 2(1) "corporate service" means: (a) "forming, on behalf of another person, a corporation or other legal person"; (b) acting,
-- or arranging for another person to act, as a director or secretary of a corporation, a partner, or in a similar capacity;
-- (c) "providing a registered office, business address, correspondence or administrative address"; (d) acting, or arranging for
-- another to act, as a nominee shareholder "other than a corporation whose securities are listed on an approved exchange";
-- (e) "carrying out any designated activity in relation to the provision of any accounting service" (designated activity
-- includes "management of client money, securities or other assets"); (f) carrying out an ACRA transaction using the electronic
-- transaction system "(i) on behalf of another person; or (ii) for one or more companies as a secretary of each".
-- s 2(2): the references include corporations, legal persons and partnerships "formed, established or incorporated outside
-- Singapore". Preparing a tax return is an accounting service (s 3(1)) but not by itself a designated activity.
DECLARE Service IS ONE OF
    `forming a company for a client`
    `forming a foreign company for a client`
    `acting as director of a client company`
    `arranging a nominee director for a client company`
    `providing a registered office address`
    `acting as nominee shareholder of an unlisted company`
    `acting as nominee shareholder of a listed company`
    `managing client money in the course of an accounting service`
    `preparing a client's tax return`
    `filing with ACRA electronically for a client`
    `filing with ACRA as secretary of the companies`
    `drafting a commercial contract for a client`

GIVEN `the service` IS A Service
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service is a corporate service` IF
    CONSIDER `the service`
    WHEN `acting as nominee shareholder of a listed company` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `preparing a client's tax return` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `drafting a commercial contract for a client` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `7 and 42 -- no business without registration`

-- s 7(1): "A person must not carry on a business in Singapore of providing any corporate service unless the person is a registered
-- corporate service provider for that type of corporate service."
-- s 7(2): an accounting entity carrying on the business of a designated activity in relation to its own accounting service "is
-- treated as registered", until its deemed registration is suspended or cancelled under s 18(2) or 19(2) or (3).
-- s 2(3)(a): a provider is not regarded as registered while its registration is suspended under s 19(2) or (3).
-- s 42(1), (2): a person already carrying on the business before s 7 commenced, who did not need to be a registered filing agent,
-- may continue for "6 months after the section 7 commencement date" or, if it applied within those 6 months, until the
-- application is granted or "finally refused or withdrawn".
-- s 7(4): $50,000 or 2 years or both, and "a further fine not exceeding $2,500 for every day or part of a day" after conviction.
DECLARE Business HAS
    `the service` IS A Service
    `carries on a business in Singapore of providing it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is registered for that type of service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `registration is suspended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an accounting entity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is within the section 42 transitional period` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the business` IS A Business
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the business is deemed registered` IF
        `the business`'s `is an accounting entity`
    AND `the business`'s `the service` EQUALS `managing client money in the course of an accounting service`
    AND (NOT `the business`'s `registration is suspended`)

GIVEN `the business` IS A Business
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the business is lawfully registered` IF
        `the business is deemed registered` `the business`
    OR  (`the business`'s `is registered for that type of service` AND (NOT `the business`'s `registration is suspended`))

GIVEN `the business` IS A Business
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `carrying on the business is an offence` IF
        `the business`'s `carries on a business in Singapore of providing it`
    AND `the service is a corporate service` (`the business`'s `the service`)
    AND (NOT `the business is lawfully registered` `the business`)
    AND (NOT `the business`'s `is within the section 42 transitional period`)

GIVEN `months since section 7 commenced` IS A NUMBER, `applied within the first 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN, `application still pending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an existing business may continue under section 42` IF
        `months since section 7 commenced` LESS THAN 6
    OR  (`applied within the first 6 months` AND `application still pending`)

GIVEN `days the offence continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for an unregistered business` MEANS 50000 PLUS 2500 TIMES `days the offence continued after conviction`

§§ `8 and 10 -- renewal window`

-- s 8(2) and s 10(2): "An application for renewal of registration must be made not earlier than 60 days before the date of expiry".
GIVEN `days before expiry` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the renewal application is not too early` IF `days before expiry` AT MOST 60

§§ `9 -- when the Registrar must refuse a corporate service provider`

-- s 9(1): the Registrar "must refuse" (a) unless the applicant is an individual or partnership registered under the Business Names
-- Registration Act 2014, a company, a limited liability partnership or a limited partnership; (b) unless (i) the applicant (an
-- individual) is a registered qualified individual, (ii) at least one partner (of a partnership, LLP or LP) is one, or (iii) the
-- applicant employs, engages or appoints at least one; (c) if satisfied any key appointment holder is not fit and proper; (d) an
-- individual who has not completed a prescribed course or training; (e) a non-individual any of whose key appointment holders has
-- not; (f) if a previous registration was "cancelled under section 19(2) or (3) less than 2 years before" the application.
-- A cancellation under s 18 (for instance for want of fitness) is not in (f).
DECLARE ApplicantForm IS ONE OF
    `an individual registered under the Business Names Registration Act`
    `an individual not registered under the Business Names Registration Act`
    `a partnership registered under the Business Names Registration Act`
    `a company`
    `a limited liability partnership`
    `a limited partnership`
    `a society`

DECLARE ProviderApplicant HAS
    `form` IS AN ApplicantForm
    `is itself a registered qualified individual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a partner is a registered qualified individual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employs a registered qualified individual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a key appointment holder is not fit and proper` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant completed the prescribed course` IS A BOOLEAN
    `every key appointment holder completed the prescribed course` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had a registration cancelled under section 19` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months since that cancellation` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the form` IS AN ApplicantForm
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the form is eligible` IF
    CONSIDER `the form`
    WHEN `an individual not registered under the Business Names Registration Act` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a society` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the form` IS AN ApplicantForm
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the form is an individual` IF
    CONSIDER `the form`
    WHEN `an individual registered under the Business Names Registration Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an individual not registered under the Business Names Registration Act` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the form` IS AN ApplicantForm
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the form has partners` IF
    CONSIDER `the form`
    WHEN `a partnership registered under the Business Names Registration Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a limited liability partnership` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a limited partnership` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the applicant` IS A ProviderApplicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant has a registered qualified individual` IF
        (`the form is an individual` (`the applicant`'s `form`) AND `the applicant`'s `is itself a registered qualified individual`)
    OR  (`the form has partners` (`the applicant`'s `form`) AND `the applicant`'s `a partner is a registered qualified individual`)
    OR  `the applicant`'s `employs a registered qualified individual`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS A ProviderApplicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the training requirement is met` IF
    IF `the form is an individual` (`the applicant`'s `form`)
    THEN `the applicant`'s `the applicant completed the prescribed course`
    ELSE `the applicant`'s `every key appointment holder completed the prescribed course`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS A ProviderApplicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must refuse the provider` IF
        (NOT `the form is eligible` (`the applicant`'s `form`))
    OR  (NOT `the applicant has a registered qualified individual` `the applicant`)
    OR  `the applicant`'s `a key appointment holder is not fit and proper`
    OR  (NOT `the training requirement is met` `the applicant`)
    OR  (`the applicant`'s `had a registration cancelled under section 19` AND `the applicant`'s `months since that cancellation` LESS THAN 24)

§§ `11 -- when the Registrar must refuse a qualified individual`

-- s 11(1): must refuse (a) if the applicant "is not or ... ceases to be a qualified individual, or has not successfully completed a
-- prescribed course or training"; (b) if satisfied the applicant is not fit and proper; (c) if a previous registration was
-- cancelled under s 21(2) or (3) less than 2 years before.
DECLARE IndividualApplicant HAS
    `meets the prescribed qualified individual criteria` IS A BOOLEAN
    `completed the prescribed course` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is not fit and proper` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had a registration cancelled under section 21` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months since the cancellation` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the individual` IS AN IndividualApplicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must refuse the individual` IF
        (NOT `the individual`'s `meets the prescribed qualified individual criteria`)
    OR  (NOT `the individual`'s `completed the prescribed course`)
    OR  `the individual`'s `is not fit and proper`
    OR  (`the individual`'s `had a registration cancelled under section 21` AND `the individual`'s `months since the cancellation` LESS THAN 24)

§§ `12 -- notifying changes`

-- s 12(1): a registered person "(other than a deemed corporate service provider or deemed registered qualified individual)" must
-- notify the Registrar of any change in the particulars in its application "within 14 days after the occurrence of the change".
-- (2): fine not exceeding $10,000.
GIVEN `is a deemed registered person` IS A BOOLEAN, `days taken to notify` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the late notice is an offence` IF
    (NOT `is a deemed registered person`) AND `days taken to notify` GREATER THAN 14

§§ `14 -- who provides the service`

-- s 14(1): a registered provider "must ensure" the service is provided by "(a) one or more registered qualified individuals; or
-- (b) one or more prescribed persons under the supervision of a registered qualified individual". Section 14 creates no offence.
GIVEN `provided by a registered qualified individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `provided by a prescribed person` IS A BOOLEAN, `supervised by a registered qualified individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service is provided as section 14 requires` IF
        `provided by a registered qualified individual`
    OR  (`provided by a prescribed person` AND `supervised by a registered qualified individual`)

§§ `16 -- nominee directors`

-- s 16(1): a provider must not arrange for a person to act as a nominee director of a company "unless the registered corporate
-- service provider is satisfied that the person is a fit and proper person". (2) In deciding, it "must (a) take all reasonable
-- steps to satisfy" itself that the person is not disqualified from acting as a director under any written law, and (b) consider
-- the prescribed factors. (3) Fine not exceeding $100,000.
-- Reading (2) as a condition of a satisfaction that counts under (1) is an inference: s 16(3) punishes failure to comply with (1).
GIVEN `arranged a nominee director` IS A BOOLEAN, `was satisfied the person is fit and proper` IS A BOOLEAN, `took reasonable steps on disqualification` IS A BOOLEAN, `considered the prescribed factors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `arranging the nominee director is an offence` IF
        `arranged a nominee director`
    AND (NOT (`was satisfied the person is fit and proper` AND `took reasonable steps on disqualification` AND `considered the prescribed factors`))

§§ `17 -- customer due diligence`

-- s 17(1): CDD must be performed "(a) before providing any corporate service to a customer"; (b) on reason to suspect money
-- laundering, proliferation financing or terrorism financing; (c) on reason to doubt earlier CDD information; (d) as prescribed.
-- (3): "Unless subsection (2) applies", the provider "may choose not to perform or complete" CDD if it suspects the transaction
-- relates to money laundering etc. AND has reason to believe performing the measures "will tip off the customer".
-- (4): where it "is for any reason unable or chooses not to complete" CDD, it must decline the service, terminate any ongoing
-- service, determine whether to make a disclosure under the CDSA s 45 or the Terrorism (Suppression of Financing) Act, and record
-- the basis. (7): fine not exceeding $100,000 for failing (1), (2), (4), (5) or (6).
GIVEN `about to provide a service to a customer` IS A BOOLEAN, `suspects money laundering or terrorism financing` IS A BOOLEAN, `doubts earlier due diligence information` IS A BOOLEAN, `a prescribed circumstance applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `customer due diligence is required` IF
        `about to provide a service to a customer`
    OR  `suspects money laundering or terrorism financing`
    OR  `doubts earlier due diligence information`
    OR  `a prescribed circumstance applies`

GIVEN `suspects the transaction relates to money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN, `believes due diligence would tip off the customer` IS A BOOLEAN, `a prescribed bar under subsection 2 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provider may skip customer due diligence` IF
        `suspects the transaction relates to money laundering`
    AND `believes due diligence would tip off the customer`
    AND (NOT `a prescribed bar under subsection 2 applies`)

GIVEN `completed customer due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provider must decline and consider a disclosure` IF NOT `completed customer due diligence`

§§ `19 and 21 -- regulatory action`

-- s 19(1): applies where a provider is contravening "(a) if Z is not a deemed registered corporate service provider -- (i) any of
-- the conditions of Z's registration; or (ii) any requirement under this Act or the regulations, the contravention of or
-- non-compliance with which is not an offence"; (b) a deemed provider -- only (ii). s 21(1) is the same for qualified individuals,
-- adding for a non-deemed individual a declaration under an ACRA Act that is "false or misleading" or that Z "was not authorised to
-- make". s 19(2), 21(2): cancel; suspend "for a period not exceeding 12 months"; restrict use of the electronic transaction system;
-- a financial penalty "not exceeding $25,000" (provider) or "$10,000" (individual) "for each contravention"; or censure.
DECLARE Contravention HAS
    `is deemed registered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `breached a condition of registration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `breached a requirement that is not an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `breached only a requirement that is an offence` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the case` IS A Contravention
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 19 applies` IF
        `the case`'s `breached a requirement that is not an offence`
    OR  ((NOT `the case`'s `is deemed registered`) AND `the case`'s `breached a condition of registration`)

DECLARE RegisteredKind IS ONE OF
    `a corporate service provider`
    `a qualified individual`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A RegisteredKind, `number of contraventions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum financial penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a corporate service provider` THEN 25000 TIMES `number of contraventions`
    WHEN `a qualified individual` THEN 10000 TIMES `number of contraventions`

GIVEN `months of suspension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suspension is within power` IF `months of suspension` AT MOST 12

§§ `23 -- appeals`

-- s 23(2): an appeal "must be made within 30 days after the date the decision appealed against is given". (4) The Minister's
-- decision "is final". (6) An appeal "does not affect the operation of the decision" and, "unless otherwise directed by the
-- Minister", the decision "must be complied with until the determination of the appeal".
GIVEN `days after the decision was given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF `days after the decision was given` AT MOST 30

GIVEN `the Minister directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision must be obeyed pending the appeal` IF NOT `the Minister directed otherwise`

§§ `7, 12, 16, 17, 25 and 27 -- offences and composition`

-- Maximum fines: s 7(4) $50,000 (or 2 years); s 12(2) $10,000; s 16(3) $100,000; s 17(7) $100,000; s 25 (false or misleading
-- information to the Registrar) $50,000 (or 2 years). s 27(1): a prescribed compoundable offence may be compounded for "a sum not
-- exceeding the lower of" "(a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine" and "(b) $20,000".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `carrying on business unregistered`
    `failing to notify a change`
    `arranging an unfit nominee director`
    `failing in customer due diligence`
    `giving false information to the Registrar`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `carrying on business unregistered` THEN 50000
    WHEN `failing to notify a change` THEN 10000
    WHEN `arranging an unfit nominee director` THEN 100000
    WHEN `failing in customer due diligence` THEN 100000
    WHEN `giving false information to the Registrar` THEN 50000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months of imprisonment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `carrying on business unregistered` THEN 24
    WHEN `giving false information to the Registrar` THEN 24
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS `the lower of` (`the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 20000
